# The joint cumulant generating function of the limiting Dickey-Fuller t-ratio (Bao, Broda and Kan,
# "Inversion formulas and saddlepoint expansions for Studentized means", Section 7): a test fixture
# for the Studentized-mean functions, not part of the package. The same code is in the
# repository of the paper (julia/DFCGF.jl).
using SaddlepointExpansions: CGF, factT
using TaylorSeries: TaylorN, constant_term

# Taylor coefficients in z = mu^2 of D1(z)/e^c (Model M2) and D2(z)/e^c (Model M3) at z = 0, as
# functions of lam = -s and c; transcribed from df_series.py (generated by sympy).  The rational
# coefficients are formed in the number type T, so that the series are correct at any precision.
rat(::Type{T}, n, d) where {T} = T(n) / T(d)
